ems to be  to act  cute and help kirito and asuna once in a  while with technical support  and don't even get me started on the  villains  kaiaba the creator of the original sao  and nerve gear seems to be interesting  at first  but as we learn more about him we  realize that his character is shallow  and his motivations for doing what he  did  make no sense i mean sure we can  understand why kaibab would want to have  full control of the virtual world he  created  power is definitely a strong motivator  for human beings  but why did kayaba decide that thousands  of innocent people needed to die  in sao he could have still controlled  the virtual world without having anyone  actually die and even if he wanted to  keep people trapped in the game he could  have held their consciousnesses captive  just like nobuyuki aka fairy king oberon  does to asuna and the others  literally no one had to die let alone  innocent teenagers who just wanted to  play a game  kaiba eventually scans his brain and  permanently transfers his consciousness  into the virtual world which is another  thought-provoking sci-fi  concept but the full potential of this  premise  is never explored and not much is done  with kaioba's character  even though there were so many  possibilities to do more  our boy fairy king oberon is also a very  one-dimensional villain he is an evil  psycho who wants money and power  but other than being extremely punchable  for the evil douchebag that he  is there is nothing relatable or complex  about his character  what drove him to become the way that he  is what is his belief system and the  true driving force behind his actions  human beings are complicated it is very  rare for someone to just be purely  evil or purely good but there is nothing  complicated about  oberon he's just an abusive psycho who  wants money and power  other villains like death gun also turn  out to be one-dimensional and their  motivations turn out to be pretty  dubious once we learn  more about them and in the ordinal scale  movie the primary villain is a professor  whose daughter died in the original sao  and he wants to revive her by stealing  all of the memories of her from the sao  survivors  he needs to steal the memories in order  to reconstruct her personality in the  virtual world  turning her into a sort of ai but if you  ask me this entire concept makes  literally no sense since the memories  that others have of the daughter could  not possibly help reconstruct her true  personality  the way that we see and perceive other  people that we meet is completely  different from the way that they see and  perceive themselves and unless you can  read minds you can't possibly know what  someone else is thinking or  feeling on the inside so stealing the  inherently subjective memories that sao  survivors have of his daughter could do  little in terms of reconstructing the  daughter's true personality  which means that the professor's entire  elaborate master plan  makes very little sense to me and this  is the main issue that i have with sao  we start off with an intriguing sci-fi  premise and main characters like kirito  and asuna that we can definitely work  with  but not nearly enough effort is spent on  developing the other characters or on  constructing a logical and compelling  plot line  each arc consists of either kirito or  asuna or both  obtaining new skills and weapons and  using them to destroy one-dimensional  unforgettable villains with some minor  help from the side characters  we always end up with a very simplistic  dynamic of good guy kirito versus a  one-dimensional villain  and of course we know that the story  will end with kirito training  obtaining new skills or weapons and then  defeating the villain  and this is unfortunate because as i  mentioned so many times in this video  sao has the potential to explore more  complex and nuanced sci-fi themes  themes that other anime like ghost in  the shell and psychopaths have explored  so successfully  and the truth is that the sao formula  may well be the future  of anime if we take a look at the surge  in isekai anime in recent years it is  clear that the goal of most of these  anime is to attract viewers with an  intriguing premise an ordinary person  just like you  ends up in a really cool fantasy world  full of women who want you  and plot twist you are also extremely  powerful despite being completely new to  this world and then once they suck  viewers in with the escapist power  fantasy premise  they spend very little effort on  character development and plot  the protagonist is always good pure  overpowered and a chick magnet and of  course his enemies are all evil  one-dimensional psychopaths who are  defeated  as soon as he finds a new more powerful  sword or spell  or nunchucks or whatever this formula  could be the future of anime because  it's easier to produce  shows of this type it's easier to create  a cool premise and then just make  formulaic arcs in which the protagonist  is kicking ass in roughly the same way  every time  only the villains and the items being  used to defeat the villains are changing  it is much harder to create a gripping  and coherent overarching plotline that  includes meaningful character  development for all the relevant cast  members  and that treats its villains as actual  multi-dimensional human beings with  complex  thoughts feelings and motivations as far  as sword art  online goes i think it gets more hate  than it deserves and i will definitely  still watch the alicization arc as it  comes out in anime form  but sao has the potential to be so  much better and we need to expect more  from franchises like  sao otherwise the future of anime will  be series with intriguing concepts that  never put in the work  necessary to achieve their full  potential and we are going to keep  seeing a bunch of bad  sao clones like isekaiwa smartphone  popping up  every new anime season at least that's  my opinion  but let me know what you guys think do  you agree with my take on  sao and the future of anime or do you  think that i'm wrong an isekaiwa  smartphone is actually a modern classic  let me know down below if you enjoyed  this video you want to see more videos  like it leave a like to let me know  if you're new to the channel don't  forget to subscribe and hit that  notification bell  also be sure to follow us on twitter and  instagram at anime uproar for all the  latest updates  and a big thank you to ac design for  editing this and other videos for us  he's doing a great job be sure to check  him out link in the description  as always thank you all so much for  watching and until next time see ya  space cowboys  [Music]
 

